{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LoJHm4byg6o17wC8AYa7eo","type":"tool_result","content":"# Ingress backed by a single Service\n\nAn Ingress backed by a single Service is the simplest Ingress configuration. It exposes a single Service to external traffic.\n\nHere is the example from the documentation:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Ingress\nmetadata:\n  name: ingress-wildcard-host\nspec:\n  host: *.example.com\n  defaultBackend:\n    service:\n      name: service1\n      port:\n        number: 80\n```\n\nNote that this YAML uses `defaultBackend` to specify the backend Service, rather than using rules."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","uuid":"c9018ab6-ef69-4b68-8963-6f88b11c65ec","timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:48:22.726Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":572977,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Ingress backed by a single Service\n\nAn Ingress backed by a single Service is the simplest Ingress configuration. It exposes a single Service to external traffic.\n\nHere is the example from the documentation:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Ingress\nmetadata:\n  name: ingress-wildcard-host\nspec:\n  host: *.example.com\n  defaultBackend:\n    service:\n      name: service1\n      port:\n        number: 80\n```\n\nNote that this YAML uses `defaultBackend` to specify the backend Service, rather than using rules.","durationMs":2953,"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/ingress/"}}
