{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ification flag on Ch 10 §4's third beat. This is the page the Ingress\n\"frozen\" Note hyperlinks to when it says the Ingress API \"is subject to the stability guarantees for\ngener"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"ab6b854f-e560-4f15-ab95-b118710ff0bf"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ally available APIs\" — the anchor is #deprecating-parts-of-the-api. It supplies the formal\nKubernetes meaning of \"deprecated\", which the chapter contrasts against \"frozen\".)\n\n## Overview"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"05c7ed37-e4aa-4b06-adc0-6b850e102d73"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nKubernetes is a large system with many components and many contributors. As with any such software, the feature set naturally evolves over time, and sometimes a feature may need to be removed. This could include"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"b64260e9-4f39-4136-a955-6eeacbdbb39d"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" an API, a flag, or even an entire feature. To avoid breaking existing users, Kubernetes follows a deprecation policy for aspects of the system that are slated to be removed.\n\n## Deprecating parts of the API"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"25ec1005-e16a-4e2b-88ca-00c6bfd4dc07"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nSince Kubernetes is an API-driven system, the API has evolved over time to reflect the evolving understanding of the problem space. The Kubernetes API is actually a set of APIs, called \"API groups\", and each API group is independently versioned.\n\nThe following r"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"4a0c3555-a62e-4b37-a569-2e00ebd90020"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ules govern the deprecation of elements of the API. This includes:\n\n- REST resources (aka API objects)\n- Fields of REST resources\n- Annotations on REST resources, including \"beta\" annotations but not including \"alpha\" annotations."}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"de29c1dd-9cb6-4354-8ca2-af245efe0870"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n- Enumerated or constant values\n- Component config structures\n\nThese rules are enforced between official releases, not between arbitrary commits to master or release branches.\n\n## Rules"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"9565e70e-1b6b-459e-a2e7-a26659b92e8d"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\n**Rule #1: API elements may only be removed by incrementing the version of the API group.**\n\nOnce an API element has been added to an API group at a particular version, it can not be removed from"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"91b610de-f26b-4107-afc5-22a0431de7fe"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" that version or have its behavior significantly changed, regardless of track.\n\n**Rule #2: API objects must be able to round-trip between API versions in a given release without information loss, with the exception of wh"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"7ee2a177-ef96-4089-9bfe-252e7739ba41"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ole REST resources that do not exist in some versions.**\n\n**Rule #3: An API version in a given track may not be deprecated in favor of a less stable API version.**\n\n- GA API versions can replace beta and alpha API versions."}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"8231d720-f7d5-4207-baea-2b6876918487"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n- Beta API versions can replace earlier beta and alpha API versions, but may not replace GA API versions.\n- Alpha API versions can replace earlier alpha API versions, but may not replace GA or beta API versions.\n\n**Rule #4a: API lifetime"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"1ff06184-9046-4604-9e0d-4663aa27c04e"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" is determined by the API stability level**\n\n- GA API versions may be marked as deprecated, but must not be removed within a major version of Kubernetes\n- Beta API versions are deprecated no more than 9 months or 3 minor releases after introduction ("}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"20dba9c6-a6ba-441d-a7be-9b50ec57a6d5"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"whichever is longer), and are no longer served 9 months or 3 minor releases after deprecation (whichever is longer)\n- Alpha API versions may be removed in any release without prior deprecation notice\n\n**"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"feb7e9f9-1046-4ade-999d-389c21e5cdd0"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"Rule #4b: The \"preferred\" API version and the \"storage version\" for a given group may not advance until after a release has been made that supports both the new version and the previous version**\n\nUsers"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"4eab397c-fead-4206-a043-e65c4bf2ce26"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" must be able to upgrade to a new release of Kubernetes and then roll back to a previous release, without converting anything to the new API version or suffering breakages (unless they explicitly used features only available in the new"}},"session_id":"087b09f1-914c-4211-8f4f-c2844f53e37c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"317f4137-bc80-43e0-8b3a-8ed0ea2a6eaf"}
